<title>USA: SPX names O'Leary as new CFO.</title>
<headline>SPX names O'Leary as new CFO.</headline>
<dateline>MUSKEGON, Mich. 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>SPX Corp said Tuesday it named Patrick O'Leary as treasurer and chief financial officer, replacing William Trubeck, who left the company.</p>
<p>O'Leary, 39 years old, was previously chief financial officer of Carlisle Plastics Inc, which was recently acquired by Tyco International Ltd.</p>
<p>The company did not provide a reason for Trubeck's departure and a spokesman was not available for comment.</p>
<p>SPX makes specialty service tools and components for the motor vehicle industry.</p>
</text>
